# Sandbox vs production

Plugin Configure `ECARTPAY_MODE` selects the **API** host. Dashboard and OAuth stay on production.

| | Sandbox (default) | Production |
|---|---|---|
| `ECARTPAY_MODE` | `sandbox` | `production` |
| API base URL | `https://sandbox.ecartpay.com` | `https://ecartpay.com` |
| Keys | Sandbox API keys (dashboard Sandbox toggle on) | Production API keys |
| Cards / transfers | Test data from docs only | Real customer payment methods |
| Dashboard / OAuth | `https://ecartpay.com` | `https://ecartpay.com` |

Rules:

1. Default all live slash-command actions and new integration work to **sandbox**.
2. Never mix sandbox keys with production hosts (or the reverse).
3. Use official test cards/transfers from https://docs.ecartpay.com/docs/test-cards-1 and related sandbox guides.
4. Warn the user explicitly before generating or running code, or MCP writes, against production.
5. Treat production keys and live webhook secrets as high-risk credentials.
6. If `ECARTPAY_BASE_URL` is set, it overrides mode. Confirm it matches the keys.
7. Prefer Cursor **Authenticate** on `ecartpay-api` (production login) or OAuth Connect for partner apps over pasting production keys into the IDE.
